    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0391" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg303"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-04-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                    1904</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Porter sends the following from Messrs. Day and Russell to the
                    Attorney-General:</p>
                <p>General deed conveying totality of property has been executed and delivered
                    before our consul-general. Deed drawn to suit us, and we are guaranteed all
                    further deeds we may want later. We are to pay transfer charges, if any. Have no
                    expectations of having to pay any. We shall take possession here and shall cable
                    Walker at Panama to take over properties there, sending copy of deed and other
                    papers.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
